Context & Technical Rationale:
The extracted crdt-contracts repo carried 4 contract tests from the monorepo;
compatGate.test.ts/compatGateDrift.test.ts shell out to scripts/compat-gate.mjs,
which was never extracted. The parent script's default contracts dir was
packages/crdt-contracts and it additionally asserted monorepo-only facts
(root/server package.json file-deps, plugin/server import sites) that have no
meaning here. The repo-local gate defaults --contracts-dir to the repo ROOT
(package now lives there) and keeps only the independent-pin checks described in
README.md: compat-manifest.protocolVersion === exported PROTOCOL_VERSION and
compat-manifest.contracts === package.json.version. Resolution stays
require(dist) -> import(src/protocol.ts) -> strict source-parse so a build is not
a precondition. This is the 'repo-local equivalent matching documented gate
semantics' option; no contract semantics were invented.

Privacy & Security Guarantees:
Read-only: the gate reads local JSON + the local compiled/source artifact and
exits. Zero network, zero credentials, no telemetry, no data egress.
